@Sergey-Lyapin 
@Alex-302

I believe the reason why the suggested rule did not work is that the website redirects based on the browser’s installed language. As a result, the consent button may appear as `acceptAll button` or `acceptAll bouton`. Because of this variation, the selector in the scriptlet does not always match. 

However, even when using both selectors, the popup still flashes briefly before disappearing. To remove the popup, the dark overlay, and the flash, without relying on `.ld_KL` and `:nth-child()`, the following user rules do work consistently :

walmart.ca##div[role="dialog"]:has(> div > div > button[aria-label*="acceptAll"])
walmart.ca##div:has(> div[role="dialog"]:has(button[aria-label*="acceptAll"]))
